    "content": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "html": "<p>At the heart of the presentation was <em>Damaged</em>, shown in its gold-leaf edition — edition one of six — from Boky's Figurative Poetry Collection. The work distills the language central to her practice: a fragmented figure whose broken surfaces are gilded rather than concealed, holding beauty and rupture within a single form. Finished in gold leaf, <em>Damaged</em> transforms absence and injury into something luminous — a quiet meditation on resilience and the poetry of the incomplete.</p>",
